From d8b44c87676a940cbd93423fa532b6a776fb96c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:41:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [WPE] Bind a network session to an uplink

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Add an uplink property to the network session that pins every connection
of a web view to a chosen interface, source address or subnet, so one
view can leave through a tunnel while others use the default route. An
interface pin binds the device only, for IPv4 and IPv6, so the kernel
picks the device's current source address per connection and an address
change during a session is followed; an address or subnet pin binds that
address, per family. A connection that cannot be pinned fails closed.

The uplink is given as "<interface|address|subnet>[;dns=<server>,...]".
When it is set, the full value is handed to uplinkdns_uplink_add() if
that symbol is present, so names resolve through the same uplink the
socket binds to; absent it, the system resolver is used. The bind runs
for every connection at the connecting stage, before connect.

